---
import WorkCaseStudyLayout from '../../../layouts/WorkCaseStudyLayout.astro';
import { profile, projectsData } from '../../../data/profileData';

const project = projectsData.find((item) => item.title === 'Automatic IoT Soap Dispenser');
if (!project) throw new Error('Automatic IoT Soap Dispenser project not found');

const siteUrl = profile.links.web.replace(/\/$/, '');
const canonical = `${siteUrl}/work/iot-soap-dispenser/`;
const socialImage = `${siteUrl}${project.image}`;
const pageTitle = 'Automatic IoT Soap Dispenser · Embedded IoT and remote monitoring · Gabriel Bibbó';
const description = 'Expanded project page for an industrial IoT handwashing system combining automatic dispensing, employee identification, cloud connectivity and remote compliance monitoring.';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  '@id': `${canonical}#webpage`,
  url: canonical,
  name: pageTitle,
  description,
  inLanguage: 'en',
  dateModified: profile.updated,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', '@id': `${siteUrl}/#person`, name: profile.name, url: `${siteUrl}/` },
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'CreativeWork',
    name: project.title,
    description: project.description,
    creator: { '@id': `${siteUrl}/#person` },
    keywords: project.tags,
    url: canonical,
  },
};
---

<WorkCaseStudyLayout
  canonical={canonical}
  socialImage={socialImage}
  pageTitle={pageTitle}
  description={description}
  schema={schema}
  eyebrow="IoT · Embedded systems · Industrial hygiene · 2020-2021"
  heading="An IoT handwashing system with remote compliance monitoring"
  intro="This project combined an automatic soap-dispensing device with employee identification and a web application for remotely monitoring handwashing records in industrial environments."
  facts={[
    { value: 'WiFi', label: 'cloud-connected device' },
    { value: 'IR / RFID', label: 'sensing and identification' },
    { value: '3 L', label: 'documented soap tank capacity' },
    { value: 'Web dashboard', label: 'remote records and administration' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Embedded device</h2>
      <p>The physical system was designed for industrial hygiene workflows. The archived project description documents a stainless-steel enclosure, WiFi connectivity, IR/RFID sensing, cloud connectivity and a three-litre soap reservoir.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <article><h3>Automatic interaction</h3><p>The dispensing workflow was designed around non-contact sensing while keeping the device suitable for repeated use in a shared workplace.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Identification</h3><p>RFID/card associations linked physical interactions to employees so that wash events could be recorded against individual users rather than only counted globally.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Connected records</h3><p>WiFi and cloud connectivity moved the project beyond a standalone dispenser, enabling wash events to become remotely inspectable operational data.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Industrial context</h3><p>The system was conceived as a complete device-and-software workflow rather than a consumer soap dispenser, with administration and compliance visibility built into the concept.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Remote management interface</h2>
      <p>The archived web application supported more than a simple event list. Its administration screens covered employees, identification cards, company sections, application users and system logs, with data export available from the maintenance views.</p>
      <div class="evidence"><div class="label">Employees</div><div>Create, modify and remove employee records, with safeguards when an employee already has associated wash data.</div></div>
      <div class="evidence"><div class="label">Cards and sections</div><div>Maintain employee cards and organisational sections, supporting a workplace-level deployment rather than an anonymous counter.</div></div>
      <div class="evidence"><div class="label">Wash history</div><div>Inspect recorded washes with employee, date, time and card information.</div></div>
      <div class="evidence"><div class="label">Missed washes</div><div>For a selected day, the interface could show employees for whom no handwashing event had been recorded.</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Device and monitoring evidence</h2>
      <div class="visual-grid">
        <figure class="figure">
          <a class="figure-frame" href={project.image} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" aria-label="Open the full-size IoT soap dispenser project image">
            <img src={project.image} alt="Automatic IoT soap dispenser project" loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <figcaption>Archived portfolio image of the physical IoT soap-dispenser project.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="figure">
          <a class="figure-frame" href="/homepage_files/case_study_iot_washes.webp" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" aria-label="Open the archived handwashing dashboard image">
            <img src="/homepage_files/case_study_iot_washes.webp" alt="Archived IoT soap dispenser dashboard showing recorded handwashing events" loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <figcaption>Archived monitoring interface showing timestamped handwashing records associated with employees and cards.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Project scope</h2>
      <p>The surviving material documents both the embedded device concept and its management software. It supports the project as an IoT systems effort spanning sensing, identification, connectivity and operational tooling; it does not establish a later production deployment, so no production-scale claim is made here.</p>
      <div class="tags">{project.tags.map((tag) => <span class="tag">{tag}</span>)}<span class="tag">Remote monitoring</span><span class="tag">Web administration</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</WorkCaseStudyLayout>
